# language: en

Feature: Signal API set

    @coldstart @serial
    Scenario Outline: Cold start once and seed initial actuator values
        Given Kura service is cleanly restarted
        When HeadlessApp sets the following actuator signals
        | path                                                     | datatype | value         |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.FuelSystem.IsFuelPortFlapOpen | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.PowerOptimizeLevel | uint8 | 5 |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Charging.StartStopCharging | string | STOP |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Number1.BatteryConditioning.TargetTemperature | float | 0.0 |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.Transmission.SelectedGear | int8 | 0 |
        
        Then PAL should report the following actuator signals
        | path                                                     | datatype | value         |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.FuelSystem.IsFuelPortFlapOpen | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.PowerOptimizeLevel | uint8 | 5 |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Charging.StartStopCharging | string | STOP |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Number1.BatteryConditioning.TargetTemperature | float | 0.0 |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.Transmission.SelectedGear | int8 | 0 |
        
    @warm @serial
    Scenario Outline: Overwrite/confirm after cold start (no restart)
        Given Set the actuator signal <path> to <datatype> <default_value>
        When HeadlessApp set the actuator signal <path> to <datatype> <checked_value>
        Then the result obtained from the actuator signal by PAL should be <datatype> <checked_value> on <path>

    Examples:
        | path                                                     | datatype | default_value | checked_value |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.FuelSystem.IsFuelPortFlapOpen | bool | false | true |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.PowerOptimizeLevel | uint8 | 5 | 10 |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Charging.StartStopCharging | string | STOP | START |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Number1.BatteryConditioning.TargetTemperature | float | 0.0 | 3.4028235e+38 |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.Transmission.SelectedGear | int8 | 0 | 127 |
        
    Scenario Outline: Millions of set requests do not kill kura server & values remain consistent
        When HeadlessApp set the signal <path> to <datatype> <checked_value> <count> times with duplex <duplex>
        Then the result obtained from the actuator signal by PAL should be <datatype> <checked_value> on <path>

    Examples:
        | path                                                     | count            | duplex           | datatype      | default_value | checked_value |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.FuelSystem.IsFuelPortFlapOpen | 20 | 10 | bool | false | true |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.PowerOptimizeLevel | 20 | 10 | uint8 | 5 | 10 |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Charging.StartStopCharging | 20 | 10 | string | STOP | START |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Number1.BatteryConditioning.TargetTemperature | 20 | 10 | float | 0.0 | 3.4028235e+38 |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.Transmission.SelectedGear | 20 | 10 | int8 | 0 | 127 |
        
    @CleanupRestoreServerforSet
    Scenario Outline: Set requests are failed when the server is stopped
        When the server is stopped for set
        Then an attempt to set the actuator signal <path> to <datatype> <checked_value> is failed

    Examples:
        | path                                                     | datatype      | checked_value       |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.FuelSystem.IsFuelPortFlapOpen | bool | true |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.PowerOptimizeLevel | uint8 | 10 |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Charging.StartStopCharging | string | START |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Number1.BatteryConditioning.TargetTemperature | float | 3.4028235e+38 |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.Transmission.SelectedGear | int8 | 127 |
        

    @CleanupRestoreNetworkforSet
    Scenario Outline: Set requests are failed when the network communication failure
        When network failure of <network_failure> is injected for set
        Then an attempt to set the actuator signal <path> to <datatype> <checked_value> is failed

    Examples:
        | path                                                     | datatype      | checked_value       | network_failure       |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.FuelSystem.IsFuelPortFlapOpen | bool | true | timeout |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.FuelSystem.IsFuelPortFlapOpen | bool | true | reject |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.PowerOptimizeLevel | uint8 | 10 | timeout |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.PowerOptimizeLevel | uint8 | 10 | reject |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Charging.StartStopCharging | string | START | timeout |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Charging.StartStopCharging | string | START | reject |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Number1.BatteryConditioning.TargetTemperature | float | 3.4028235e+38 | timeout |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.TractionBattery.Number1.BatteryConditioning.TargetTemperature | float | 3.4028235e+38 | reject |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.Transmission.SelectedGear | int8 | 127 | timeout |
        | Vehicle.Powertrain.Transmission.SelectedGear | int8 | 127 | reject |
        